# cpmtools diskdef for the official Regnecentralen RC759 "Piccoline" DR C
# diskettes (datamuseum.dk IMD blobs). Verified against bits 30005869
# ("DR C v.1.11"): 77 cyl x 2 heads, 8x1024 B/track, CP/M-86 filesystem,
# block 2048, 2 reserved cylinders (boottrk 4 -> dir @ 0x8000).
# NB: this cpmtools build reads ./diskdefs from the CWD (DISKDEFS env ignored).
#
# FIXED 2026-08-18 (bug found 2026-08-17): maxdir was WRONGLY 96/os 2.2. The
# real RC759 CCP/M-86 / DR C floppy directory is 512 entries, os 3 (CP/M-3
# datestamp SFCBs in every 4th slot, across TWO 8 KB dir blocks) -- verified on
# raw DDHF disks 30002664/30002725. maxdir 96 under-reads (misses entries past
# slot 96) and, worse, a cpmcp WRITE with too-small maxdir reserves too few
# directory blocks and scribbles file data over the real 2nd dir block,
# corrupting the disk (root cause of the levee SDIR garbage, ravn/mame#25).
# Canonical copy of this corrected diskdef (name swapped for clarity):
# open-watcom-v2/contrib/ravn/owc-drc/diskdefs, diskdef `drc-rc759`. Kept the
# NAME `rc759-drc` here (content only fixed) so existing `-f rc759-drc`
# callers in this tree keep working but now get the correct geometry.
diskdef rc759-drc
  seclen 1024
  tracks 154
  sectrk 8
  blocksize 2048
  maxdir 512
  skew 1
  boottrk 4
  os 3
end

# SW1400 CCP/M-86 r3.1 system distribution disk (datamuseum.dk 30004107,
# disk1.imd). Same geometry as rc759-drc but 160 directory entries (per the
# datamuseum auto-analysis signature "1024_2048_0x0_*1+1_2:0_76:1_160") --
# using rc759-drc's maxdir=96 against this disk falsely reports "directory
# full" once >96 files exist even though free blocks remain.
diskdef sw1400-sys
  seclen 1024
  tracks 154
  sectrk 8
  blocksize 2048
  maxdir 160
  boottrk 4
  os 3
end
